#14135
Entrance to the Cathedral~
It would seem this immense chamber was once a cathedral, great sweeping archs
in the ceiling would seem to suggest that. Bronze braziers hang from golden
chains, shedding a dim light and giving of a heady incense that makes the air
hazy. The floor here seems worn, as if by the passing of many feet. The hall
continues to the east, north and south, while a stone corridor leads west out
of the chamber.
~
