#14147
Frescos~
Your at the southern edge of the Cathedral. There are paintings on the walls,
here in quite good condition. Depicted is a small, but busy tavern. Musicians
can be seen, playing the flute and the harp, while a beautitfull woman appears
to be singing to a captive audience. To the far left, you can just see the
sign of the tavern through a window. It's difficult to tell due to the angle,
but the sign seems to display a shining sun. The hall continues to the west
and north, while a small chamber lies off to the east.
~
